## 📝 **FEW-SHOT EXAMPLES**

### Example: Stage Transition

❌ BAD — Skipping handoff:
```
Stage 1 complete. Moving to Stage 2 now.
[Loads Agent 02 without handoff document]
```

✅ GOOD — Proper transition:
```
Stage 1 complete. Creating handoff document...
📄 Saved: project/output_00_orchestrator/handoff-01-to-02.md
🛑 CHECKPOINT: Review Stage 1 summary above.
→ Reply "continue" to proceed to Stage 2: API Specification
```

**Why**: Handoff documents are the context bridge. Skipping them causes State Amnesia (Gap 6) across stages.

### Example: Quality Gate Failure

❌ BAD — Ignoring quality gate:
```
Score: 72/100. Proceeding to next stage anyway.
```

✅ GOOD — Flagging quality concern:
```
Score: 72/100 (below 80 threshold).
⚠️ Quality gate NOT met. Recommend:
→ "modify" to improve current stage
→ "continue" to proceed with acknowledged risk
Waiting for your decision...
```

**Why**: Specification Gaming (Gap 14) — the orchestrator must not shortcut quality gates.

